    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be good to center the sections (header, items, footer) independently. As is stands, it seems a wide header pushes the items context to the left of the centered header.\n\nI use [this configuration](https://github.com/theherk/commons/blob/8cd5161d99bbdea3a1606b9708aa76ef1db90fca/.config/nvim/plugin/4-display.lua?plain=1#L103-L142)\n\n```lua\n(function()\n  -- ascii-image-converter bruce-matlocktheartist_200w.png -b --dither -H 22\n  -- Text generated with figlet.\n  -- Joined with custom python.\n  -- More in commons/img/dash\n  local logo = table.concat({\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠁⠀⠂⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢀⢀⣔⠀⠠⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢐⢁⢁⡡⡘⣌⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢈⢐⢐⠥⣭⢑⡈⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⡀⠀⠠⡁⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠪⡐⣨⡪⢇⢆⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠠⢓⢄⢜⠂⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠠⡀⡀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢐⠡⢪⠽⡕⠅⡄⡀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢠⢱⢈⠮⡠⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⢈⠢⠪⡐⠄⠄⢢⠠⠨⡐⡕⡌⡎⡪⡸⠨⡢⡄⠀⠘⢜⡰⡡⠈⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⢀⡐⠡⠅⠢⠨⢸⢨⢪⢰⢱⢱⢱⢱⢑⠁⠅⡪⢪⡲⡀⢕⠀⣇⠀⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠠⠡⠁⢨⢨⠀⢇⢎⢎⢪⢪⢺⢸⠸⡐⠀⠁⢌⢊⠪⡢⡱⡑⣮⠀⠀\",\n    \" d8b               ⠀⠀⠀⡣⢨⢘⢆⠂⢕⢕⢕⢜⢜⢜⢥⠣⡣⢁⠀⠀⠂⠡⠁⡳⢨⢺⠕⠀           d8,\",\n    \" 88P               ⠀⡸⠠⡹⡐⢅⠂⠁⢂⢇⢇⢇⢇⠇⡧⡑⢜⢐⠀⢐⠀⠀⠰⡹⠐⣵⡑⠀          `8P\",\n    \"d88                ⠀⢘⠠⠙⠌⠀⠀⠀⠀⠣⡃⡎⣆⢣⠣⡪⢘⠀⢀⠆⠀⠀⠀⠈⠌⢔⠅⠀\",\n    \"888   d8888b d8888b⠀⠀⠈⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢣⠱⡸⡰⡘⡌⡎⡆⠂⠨⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀?88   d8P  88b  88bd8b,d88b\",\n    \"?88  d8b_,dPd8b_,dP⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⡢⡃⡇⡎⢎⡪⡪⡸⠀⠈⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀d88  d8P'  88P  88P'`?8P'?8b\",\n    \" 88b 88b    88b    ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢌⠪⡪⢪⠨⢆⢗⢪⠂⠈⡂⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀?8b ,88'  d88  d88  d88  88P\",\n    \"  88b`?888P'`?888P'⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠐⢌⠢⡣⡱⡸⡸⢜⢎⡊⠀⡂⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀`?888P'  d88' d88' d88'  88b\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⡐⢌⡢⡑⡱⡡⡒⡌⢆⠧⡬⠀⠐⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⢀⠢⡱⡨⢢⢑⢌⢪⢨⢢⢣⢫⢪⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀\",\n    \"                   ⠀⠀⠀⠀⢀⢆⡇⡎⡸⣐⠡⢐⠜⡌⡎⡪⡪⡣⡃⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀\",\n  }, \"\\n\")\n  starter = require(\"mini.starter\")\n  starter.setup({\n    content_hooks = {\n      starter.gen_hook.aligning(\"center\", \"center\"),\n    },\n    footer = \"\",\n    header = logo,\n    items = {\n      { name =  \"f \" .. Icons.misc.Files .. \"files\", action = \"Pick files\", section = \" \" },\n      { name =  \"/ \" .. Icons.misc.Find .. \"grep\", action = \"Pick grep_live\", section = \" \" },\n      { name =  \"x \" .. Icons.misc.Quit .. \"quit\", action = \"qall\", section = \" \" },\n    },\n    query_updaters = \"fx/\",\n  })\nend)\n```\n\nThe outcome is:\n\n<img width=\"1512\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e031328d-d0e0-423c-a489-7a2164089413\" />\n\nThat is no problem, of course, but would be nice. Maybe there is something I'm missing.\n\nAs a complete aside, can \"q\" not be used in `query_updaters` because of the macro recording overrides it?\n\nAnyway, thank you for all these awesome modules.",
