    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAligning individual section was already discussed in #832. I personally don't this is a good idea to do by default (mostly because it is not robust enough and can lead to \"crooked\" visuals), but it is possible to achieve the look by creating custom hooks. There recently was [an example of such setup](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/36#discussioncomment-11827784) shared which can be a good starting point here.\n\n> As a complete aside, can \"q\" not be used in `query_updaters` because of the macro recording overrides it?\n\nYou can set [`config.query_updaters`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/855fdb116408085b7a00be8511c566cdc33648b7/doc/mini-starter.txt#L241-L244) to whichever keys you find more appropriate.\n\nClosing as not planned.",
